coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder exit-node server [flags]

  Run an exit node

  Run an exit node replica. The replica registers with coderd using its token,
  joins the tailnet at a deterministic address derived from its exit node and
  replica IDs, and accepts HTTP CONNECT requests from workspace agents on the
  listen port. Agents older than API 2.14 cannot consume replica-aware
  configurations. Restart workspaces on the new agent before binding exit nodes.
  Send SIGHUP to reload the policy file.

OPTIONS:
      --primary-access-url url, $CODER_PRIMARY_ACCESS_URL
          URL to communicate with coderd. This should match the access URL of
          the Coder deployment.

      --token string, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_TOKEN
          Authentication token for the exit node, as printed by 'coder exit-node
          create'.

      --block-direct-connections bool, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_BLOCK_DIRECT
          Force all agent traffic through DERP relays.

      --listen-port int, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_LISTEN_PORT (default: 3128)
          Tailnet port to accept CONNECT requests on.

      --policy string, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_POLICY
          Path to the YAML policy file. Reloaded on SIGHUP.

      --prometheus-address string, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_PROMETHEUS_ADDRESS
          Address to serve Prometheus metrics on. Disabled when empty.

      --provisional-host-allow bool, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_PROVISIONAL_HOST_ALLOW
          Allow host-based allow rules to provisionally match IP-literal targets
          before sniffing. This weakens host enforcement and may permit traffic
          before the host is verified.

      --replica-id string
          Replica ID override. By default a fresh ID is generated at startup.

      --upstream-dns string-array, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_UPSTREAM_DNS
          Upstream DNS server as ip[:port]. May be repeated. Configures both
          CONNECT hostname resolution and DNS streams. By default, the exit
          node's own resolver view decides what a name means.

      --verbose bool, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_VERBOSE
          Output debug-level logs.

      --wireguard-endpoint string-array, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_WIREGUARD_ENDPOINTS
          Public ip:port of this node's WireGuard listener, advertised to agents
          so they exempt it from egress enforcement. May be repeated.

      --wireguard-listen-port int, $CODER_EXIT_NODE_WIREGUARD_LISTEN_PORT (default: 0)
          Fixed local UDP port for WireGuard. Use with --wireguard-endpoint. 0
          picks a random port.

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
